From: Alan Shearer
Subject: ipv4: UnblockSource/DropSSM must remove the source address

UnblockSource() and DropSSM() copied BlockSource()/AddSSM() and call
AddressSet::Add() after confirming the source is present. Add() is a
no-op when the address is already in the set, so IP_UNBLOCK_SOURCE and
IP_DROP_SOURCE_MEMBERSHIP never change the filter.

Remove the source instead. A second unblock/drop then returns
EADDRNOTAVAIL, which is the POSIX result.

Also initialize MulticastGroupInterface::fFilterMode to kInclude.
IsEmpty() treats anything else as a live group, so a failed JoinGroup()
could LeaveGroup() a membership that was never joined.

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/multicast.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/multicast.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/multicast.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/multicast.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/multicast.cpp
@@ -34,8 +34,9 @@
 	:
 	fParent(parent),
 	fMulticastAddress(address),
-	fInterface(interface)
+	fInterface(interface),
+	fFilterMode(kInclude)
 {
 }
 
 
@@ -89,8 +90,8 @@
 	if (!fAddresses.Has(sourceAddress))
 		return EADDRNOTAVAIL;
 
-	fAddresses.Add(sourceAddress);
+	fAddresses.Remove(sourceAddress);
 	return B_OK;
 }
 
 
@@ -114,7 +115,7 @@
 	if (!fAddresses.Has(sourceAddress))
 		return EADDRNOTAVAIL;
 
-	fAddresses.Add(sourceAddress);
+	fAddresses.Remove(sourceAddress);
 	return B_OK;
 }
